                <pb facs="0188" n="138" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav03/pg138"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 811.142/4451</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Archangel</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cole</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Archangel</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-08-15T16:00:00+04:31"><hi rendition="#italic">August 15,
                                1918, 4 p.m.</hi></date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 27, 9.51
                        p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>104. [Your] August 2, 3 [4] p.m. Nine hundred and twenty-nine tons of flax
                    certain, also other cargo about which several telegrams already sent. Port now
                    under absolute Allied control.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cole</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
